SECTION | KEY | VALUE
------------------------------
# toolbar.pdl - the fixed header menus of this window, written like #.desktop/livedesk_taskbar.pdl (TASKBAR-MENUS-DATA-DRIVEN.md): flat SECTION keys, no rebuild to change a row.
# Reader: &.widgits/_shared-lib/petslike_toolbar.c. Template: the repeat blocks (tab bar, and the pre / fixed / post rows in the rail).
#   tab_<N>_cell / tab_<N>_label            a fixed toolbar tab (cell x = tab id tb-x). None here: the pals (book) and rooms (page) tabs are in the template, their rows come from the op.
#   <cell>_menu_<N>_label / _cmd            a dropdown row of that cell
#   <cell>_menu_pre_<N>_* / _post_<N>_*     rows before / after the list the op builds (book = the pals, page = the rooms), like the taskbar's pals_menu_pre / pals_menu_post
#   _cmd:  op:<verb and args> = this app's op verb (newpal, newroom ...) | empty = just close | anything else = a shell string, run as written
# Pets are pals: ONE menu. The pals list, then + new pal / remove / cancel.
SECTION | book_menu_post_1_label   | + new pal
SECTION | book_menu_post_1_cmd     | op:fire newpal
SECTION | book_menu_post_2_label   | - remove last pal
SECTION | book_menu_post_2_cmd     | op:fire delpal
SECTION | book_menu_post_3_label   | - cancel -
SECTION | book_menu_post_3_cmd     |
SECTION | page_menu_post_1_label   | + new room
SECTION | page_menu_post_1_cmd     | op:fire newroom
SECTION | page_menu_post_2_label   | - cancel -
SECTION | page_menu_post_2_cmd     |
